                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "This is an average hidden objects game with decent artwork and on the short side. The story starts with a couple, Amanda and her fiance who are on the way to her old family house to get her wedding dress. On the way, they were attacked by a mysterious man who kidnapped her husband, turned out he is none other than the 'lone miner' who the town people thought he was just a legend.\nhttps://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=1560806000\n\nThere were so many hidden objects scenes, a recycled one which you revisit and find the same items you already took in the previous scene is there again. Puzzles were quite easy to solve without skipping. The good thing about this game you can skip both puzzles and hidden objects scenes if you are just in for the story and adventure. \nhttps://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=1560804530\n\nVoice overs were not bad, music was ok too although there were only a few tracks. The journal was good, keeping track of the story and the map is interactive. Luckily I did not encounter the bug people been talking about in the [url=https://steamcommunity.com/app/665510/discussions/0/1500126447395803281/]discussion section[/url]  \nhttps://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=1560804395\n\nPros:\n+Fast travel map.\n+Beautiful art and locations.\n+Avarege story.\n+OK music.\n+Good journal, keeping track of the story.\n+Multiple hidden objects scenes (Mix between the usual list of items and Silhouette)\n+Not bad voice-overs.\n+Variety of puzzles.\n\n\n Cons:\n-Short game.\n-No steam achievements.\n-No Bonus chapter.\n\nThis game is playable, not the best HOG but it is not the worst, can be finished in two hours. I recommend it only if you get it in a bundle or a big discount. \n\n[quote]𝐹𝑜𝑟 𝑚𝑜𝑟𝑒 𝑟𝑒𝑣𝑖𝑒𝑤𝑠 𝑐𝘩𝑒𝑐𝑘 𝑚𝑦 𝑐𝑢𝑟𝑎𝑡𝑜𝑟 𝑝𝑎𝑔𝑒 [url=http://store.steampowered.com/curator/32399565/]𝐹𝑒𝑒𝑛𝑎'𝑠 𝐶𝘩𝑜𝑖𝑐𝑒[/url][/quote]",
